This license covers Orbit: its source code, icons, text, translations and
everything else in this repository that is not listed under "Other people's
work" below (together, "the Software").

The Software is source-available, not open source. It is published so that
people can see how it works and use it, not so that they can take it.

1. What you may do

   a. Read and study the source code.
   b. Download, install, update and use the official releases published by
      the copyright holder (on this repository's Releases page, and the
      updates Orbit installs itself).
   c. Build the Software from this source code and run that build on your
      own devices.
   d. Fork this repository on GitHub, as GitHub's Terms of Service allow,
      in order to propose changes back to it (issues and pull requests).
      A contribution you send is licensed to the copyright holder under the
      same terms as the Software, with the right to use and relicense it.
   e. Quote short excerpts of the source code (a few lines) when discussing
      or reporting on the Software, with a link back to this repository.

2. What you may not do

   a. Copy, publish, share, sell, rent, sublicense or otherwise distribute
      the Software or any part of it, in source or compiled form, modified
      or not (apart from what section 1 allows).
   b. Publish, distribute or offer a modified version, a derivative work, or
      any software, app, installer or website built from the Software or
      substantial parts of it.
   c. Present the Software, or any part or modified version of it, as your
      own work, or remove, hide or change the copyright notices, the author
      credits or this license.
   d. Offer the Software, or any part of it, as part of a paid product or
      service.
   e. Use the names "Orbit" or "NovaLabs", their icons or the Software's look
      in a way that suggests your work is the Software or comes from its
      author.
   f. Use the Software's source code or text to train, fine-tune or evaluate
      machine-learning models.

   Anything not expressly allowed in section 1 is not allowed. For anything
   else (a redistribution, a port, a commercial use), ask the copyright
   holder for written permission first.

3. Other people's work

   Parts of the Software that belong to others stay under their own
